    public const POEM_LINES = 'The wind comes down from the north
with the whole desert in its pockets.
It powders the louvres, the Bible,
my mother’s good wrapper on the line.

It comes for my lips next,
    takes the water from them first,
        then the words.

Mama rubs shea into my hands
as if she is oiling a hinge,
as if I am a door
    that might not open.

And I am home,
    and dry,
        and saying nothing.';

    public const MIDPOEM = 'The house stops talking at midnight.
The fridge forgets its one long note,
    the gate stops worrying its chain.

I sit with the lamp
the way you sit with someone
    who is almost asleep,

and I write it all down
before the morning
    tells me it was nothing.';

